  out: audio_out (stereo) · curve.out (automatic)
params (written 2026-11-06; the config line above, every item kept, ranges added):
  BODY    model [tine, reed, felt, upright, honky, grand] def tine · decay 0.3..20 s def 3.5 · release 0.02..4 s def 0.4 · resonance 0..1 def 0.3
  STRIKE  hardness 0..1 def 0.45 · brightness 0..1 def 0.5 · bell 0..1 def 0.35 (the tine's or reed's ring)
  MOVE    trem 0..1 def 0.25 · tremRate 0.5..12 Hz def 4.5 · tremSync [free, 1/4, 1/8, 1/8 t, 1/16]
  OUT     drive 0..1 def 0.15 · width 0..1 def 0.6 · level 0..1 def 0.7
  STRING+ stringDetune 0..1 def 0.15 · stretch 0..1 def 0.5 (inharmonicity) · sympathetic 0..1 def 0.3
  PLAY    pedal on/off (CC64) · velCurve 0..1 · keyOff 0..1 (key-off thump) · pedalNoise 0..1
  MIC     micX 0..1 · micY 0..1 · lid 0..1 (grand)
  face (12): model · hardness brightness bell · decay release resonance · trem tremRate · drive width level — the rest behind More depth ▸
signal_dag (per note; voices from the kit's voice handling):
  note + velocity → hammer (velocity → hardness, a short felt pulse) → modal-resonator (tine + tonebar, or reed: stretched partials, bell = partials 3 and 7)
  hammer → karplus-string (felt, upright, honky, grand: 1–3 strings, stringDetune apart, stretch = inharmonicity B per register)
  modal-resonator | karplus-string → filter-svf (brightness, opened by velocity) → env-adsr (decay while held, release on key up; pedal holds)
  karplus-string (undamped strings while the pedal is down, sympathetic) → sum
  sum → modal-resonator (body: soundboard or the tine's pickup, made from modes — no recorded body) → saturator-tube (drive)
  lfo (tremRate, synced or free) → stereo-tools (tremolo: pan L↔R by trem) → level → out
decisions (2026-11-06):
  - modelled live, no sample library (No toys): tine and reed are modal; strings are Karplus–Strong with stretch; the body is modes, not a
    recorded impulse response
  - the lofi keys are the tine, reed and felt models with Tremolo and Drive; Tape Memory after it gives the wear
  - a tool made of its components wired (Axiom 3); open as components gives the same chain
open gaps (none hidden):
  - three components to build first, each proving its own numbers: modal-resonator · karplus-string · saturator-tube
  - the tests line above (12th partial sharp by 10–30 c; sympathetic energy ≥ −50 dB; a 64-voice chord in budget) stands as acceptance
  - packs: the factory names above, ≥ 6 presets each, not written yet · his yes on the UI preview (piano.ui.md)

